\newlabel{sec:pretraining-loss}{{5}{12}{Pretraining: loss and evaluation, chapter 5.1}{section.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The pretraining data and optimization paths. Split the corpus before forming overlapping windows, tokenize each split with the same fixed tokenizer, and shift each window by one position to obtain input IDs $x$ and target IDs $y$. Cross-entropy (CE) compares the logits with the targets. Only the training branch computes gradients and updates parameters. Validation uses the same current parameters in evaluation mode, with dropout disabled and no gradient recording. If the tokenizer is learned from the course corpus, fit it only on the training split.}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pretraining-flow}{{5}{12}{The pretraining data and optimization paths. Split the corpus before forming overlapping windows, tokenize each split with the same fixed tokenizer, and shift each window by one position to obtain input IDs $x$ and target IDs $y$. Cross-entropy (CE) compares the logits with the targets. Only the training branch computes gradients and updates parameters. Validation uses the same current parameters in evaluation mode, with dropout disabled and no gradient recording. If the tokenizer is learned from the course corpus, fit it only on the training split}{figure.5}{}}
